+## 2. Verified reviewed behavioral constants (from the real files)
+
+### Runner tier config
+From `task976_zb5_runner.py :: tier_config(tier)`:
+
+| tier | workload_duration_s | requests | concurrency | scanner_workers | internal_deadline_s | shell_timeout_s |
+|------|--------------------|----------|-------------|-----------------|---------------------|-----------------|
+| 1    | 120                | 240      | 2           | 1               | 180                 | 240             |
+| 2    | 120                | 720      | 6           | 2               | 240                 | 300             |
+| 3    | 90                 | 1080     | 10          | 3               | 240                 | 300             |
+
+### Worker plan
+From `task976_zb5_worker.py :: worker_plan(tier)`:
+
+| tier | bars per worker | worker hard deadline/alarm |
+|------|-----------------|----------------------------|
+| 1    | 252             | 75s                        |
+| 2    | 252             | 75s                        |
+| 3    | 504             | 75s                        |
+
+For tier 3 the per-worker bar workload is **exactly 2× the tier-2 bar workload**, while the per-worker hard deadline is **unchanged at 75 seconds**.
+
+### Runner worker collection timeout
+The runner collects each child worker with:
+
+- `proc.communicate(timeout=75)`
+
+That 75-second collection timeout is the effective ceiling for how long the runner will wait for a worker to emit its JSON evidence.
+
+For tier 3, the runner requires **exactly 3** worker evidence rows in `require_worker_evidence(...)`.
+
+### Worker safety constraints kept unchanged
+The worker still enforces:
+- exact 23-symbol canonical set + canonical hash,
+- `provider_calls == 0`,
+- `broker_calls == 0`,
+- `orders_submitted == 0`,
+- `lab_walk_calls > 0`,
+- `0 < duration_seconds <= 75`,
+- exact expected bars per symbol for the tier.
+
+These fail-closed rules have **not** been weakened in this diagnostic pass.
+
+## 3. What the live ZB5 result actually showed
+
+From the reviewed ZB5R3 evidence:
+
+- Tier 1: PASS
+- Tier 2: PASS
+- Tier 3: **FAIL — worker evidence count mismatch**
+
+No full Tier-3 metrics payload was produced.
+
+That failure mode is consistent with a runner-side collection problem where it did **not** receive exactly 3 valid worker rows for tier 3.
+
+## 4. Phase A — diagnostic instrumentation conclusion
+
+The diagnostic evidence supports this working hypothesis:
+
+Tier 3 uses **504 bars per symbol per worker**, with **23 symbols per worker**, and **3 workers**, but keeps the same **75-second** hard deadline and 75-second runner collection timeout that tier 2 uses with **252 bars per symbol per worker**.
+
+So tier 3 keeps the same per-worker CPU-time architecture while trying to do roughly **2× the deterministic work per worker** in the same wall-clock bound.
+
+If the deterministic scan workload scales roughly with bars-per-symbol, this is the most direct structural inconsistency visible in the reviewed tooling.
+
+## 5. Phase B — required offline suite status (COMPLETED)
+
